Compares Zendesk ticket with the incoming request before the process starts.

Added 2 new Zendesk API calls; Show Ticket and Show User. The Show Ticket call does not return the user's email or name, just an id. This is why the 2nd call is necessary.

The Zendesk API does not return the custom fields in a nice way, they are shown in a `custom_fields` object like so:

```
"custom_fields": [
  {
    "id": "1",
    "value": "passport_number name date_of_birth"
  },
  {
    "id": "2",
    "value": null
  }
]
```

i.e you don't know what the field is called unless you look up the ID. Have done this using environment variables, and if there is no value we get `null`. The field is always returned in the request regardless if it is empty or not.

